# Authorised keys for smores@smortress (design #748, Entry).
#
# Ignition inlines this file to /var/lib/homelab/.ssh/authorized_keys, which is
# the AuthorizedKeysFile the sshd drop-in sets. bootc does not reconcile /var, so
# an image-baked copy would never appear on an installed host and a hand-written
# one would drift; the Ignition entry is the delivery path that survives an
# upgrade. The directory and the file are owned by smores because sshd reads this
# file with the target user's uid.
#
# No key is committed here. The FIDO2 resident handle is generated with the token
# and cannot exist in the repository, so this file ships with nothing but these
# instructions: sshd authenticates nobody until a key line is appended, and that
# is the intended failure direction, not an oversight. Section 42 of
# docs/manual-steps.md has the commands:
#
#   ssh-keygen -O resident -O no-touch-required -t ed25519-sk -f ~/.ssh/id_smortress
#   printf 'no-touch-required %s\n' "$(cat ~/.ssh/id_smortress.pub)" \
#     >>ignition/smortress-authorized-keys
#
# The `no-touch-required` option is what keeps the docked token from asking for a
# touch; sshd carries no `PubkeyAuthOptions verify-required`, so the per-key
# option is the whole policy. The existing file key is the other half of the
# pair (Access token AND key) and belongs on its own line, without that option:
#
#   cat ~/.ssh/id_smortress-access.pub >>ignition/smortress-authorized-keys
#
# Append to the working copy for a fresh install, render, then
# `git checkout -- ignition/smortress-authorized-keys`; on a running host append
# to /var/lib/homelab/.ssh/authorized_keys instead. Never commit the resulting
# lines and never put a private key in this file: this file has to stay
# instructions-only, because scripts/check-server-image.sh fails on any
# non-comment line here and on any sk- resident handle in the tree, and a
# handle in git would be re-delivered to every later install by an Ignition
# config that no longer matches the token it was made with.
